# A compact function goes through the short schedule of generic versions: nothing says that it runs, so nothing is tried on it. Here no call is taken in.
# The same body takes the call in where two functions call it: such a function may run. The callee is no larger than its call, so it is taken in where code runs seldom too.
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: check=VerifyEachPass limit=MaxWarmCodeValues:1 only-passes=EstimateHeat,SummarizeForInlining,InlineCalls
# RUN: pipeline InlineCalls

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0

function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="sink" [isFreeName]
    v2 = NewClosure function=f1
    v3 = NewClosure function=f3
    v4 = NewClosure function=f4
    v5 = Call v1, -, v2, v3, v4
    Return v5
}

